      "text": "To solve the problem, we need to determine the function \\( f(x) \\) that satisfies the given functional equation:\n\\[ f(x) + 2f(1 - x) = 3x^2. \\]\nWe are asked to find \\( f(3) \\).\n\nLet's start by substituting \\( x = 3 \\) into the equation:\n\\[ f(3) + 2f(1 - 3) = 3 \\cdot 3^2, \\]\nwhich simplifies to:\n\\[ f(3) + 2f(-2) = 27. \\]\nSo we have the equation:\n\\[ f(3) + 2f(-2) = 27. \\tag{1} \\]\n\nNext, let's substitute \\( x = -2 \\) into the original equation:\n\\[ f(-2) + 2f(1 - (-2)) = 3(-2)^2, \\]\nwhich simplifies to:\n\\[ f(-2) + 2f(3) = 12. \\]\nSo we have the equation:\n\\[ f(-2) + 2f(3) = 12. \\tag{2} \\]\n\nNow we have a system of linear equations:\n1. \\( f(3) + 2f(-2) = 27 \\)\n2. \\( f(-2) + 2f(3) = 12 \\)\n\nWe can solve this system by expressing \\( f(-2) \\) from equation (2) and substituting it into equation (1). From equation (2), we can solve for \\( f(-2) \\):\n\\[ f(-2) = 12 - 2f(3). \\]\nSubstitute \\( f(-2) = 12 - 2f(3) \\) into equation (1):\n\\[ f(3) + 2(12 - 2f(3)) = 27, \\]\nwhich simplifies to:\n\\[ f(3) + 24 - 4f(3) = 27, \\]\n\\[ -3f(3) + 24 = 27, \\]\n\\[ -3f(3) = 3, \\]\n\\[ f(3) = -1. \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( f(3) \\) is \\(\\boxed{-1}\\).",
