      "text": "To solve for \\( f(3) \\), we start by using the given functional equation:\n\\[ f(x) + 2f(1 - x) = 3x^2. \\]\n\nFirst, substitute \\( x = 3 \\) into the equation:\n\\[ f(3) + 2f(1 - 3) = 3(3)^2. \\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[ f(3) + 2f(-2) = 27. \\tag{1} \\]\n\nNext, substitute \\( x = -2 \\) into the original equation:\n\\[ f(-2) + 2f(1 - (-2)) = 3(-2)^2. \\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[ f(-2) + 2f(3) = 12. \\tag{2} \\]\n\nNow we have a system of linear equations:\n1. \\( f(3) + 2f(-2) = 27, \\)\n2. \\( f(-2) + 2f(3) = 12. \\)\n\nWe can solve this system by eliminating \\( f(-2) \\). Multiply the second equation by 2:\n\\[ 2f(-2) + 4f(3) = 24. \\tag{3} \\]\n\nSubtract equation (1) from equation (3):\n\\[ (2f(-2) + 4f(3)) - (f(3) + 2f(-2)) = 24 - 27. \\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[ 3f(3) = -3, \\]\nso\n\\[ f(3) = -1. \\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( f(3) \\) is \\(\\boxed{-1}\\).",
